# Types of Insects

## Coleoptera (Beetles)
- ~400,000 species — largest order
- Hardened forewings (elytra)
- Chewing mouthparts
- Ladybirds, weevils, scarabs

## Lepidoptera (Butterflies & Moths)
- ~180,000 species
- Scaled wings, coiled proboscis
- Complete metamorphosis
- Butterflies, skippers, moths

## Hymenoptera (Ants, Bees, Wasps)
- ~150,000 species
- Two pairs of membranous wings
- Many social; ovipositor or sting
- Honeybees, bumblebees, fire ants

## Diptera (Flies)
- ~125,000 species
- One pair of wings; hind pair = halteres
- Sponging or piercing mouthparts
- Mosquitoes, house flies, hoverflies

## Hemiptera (True Bugs)
- ~80,000 species
- Piercing-sucking mouthparts
- Half-membranous forewings
- Aphids, cicadas, bed bugs

## Orthoptera (Grasshoppers & Crickets)
- ~20,000 species
- Enlarged hind legs for jumping
- Stridulating song, tympanal ears
- Locusts, katydids, mole crickets

## Odonata (Dragonflies & Damselflies)
- ~6,000 species
- Two pairs of large transparent wings
- Aerial predators; aquatic nymphs
- Dragonflies, damselflies

## Isoptera (Termites)
- ~3,000 species
- Soft-bodied, social, caste system
- Cellulose eaters via gut symbionts
- Subterranean, drywood, Formosan

## Other notable orders
### Blattodea
- Cockroaches
### Mantodea
- Praying mantises
### Phthiraptera
- Lice — ectoparasites
### Siphonaptera
- Fleas — wingless, jumping
